    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d9">

                <pb facs="0103" n="8" sameAs="frus:frus1936v04/pg8"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/7635: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Counselor of Embassy in China</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Peck</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-01-10T10:00:00+08:00">January 10, 1936—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received January 10—7:45 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>10. The Soviet Ambassador told me last night he had received information that the
                    Japanese intend very shortly to land troops at <pb facs="0104" n="9"
                        xml:id="pg9"/> Foochow and Tsingtau. Jabin Hsu of the Ministry of Finance
                    could not confirm this but said the Japanese are tampering with naval officers
                    under Admiral Shen, the mayor of Tsingtau, in effort to bring about declaration
                    of autonomy by the Tsingtau Special Municipality. Repeated to Peiping.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Peck</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
